# C# author style (LewdventureServer)

Canonical source: `.ai-factory/rules/csharp-author-style.mdc`. Keep both files in sync.

Stack: C#, ASP.NET Core, Newtonsoft.Json. Match surrounding files; for new code follow these rules.

## Language and access

- Prefer `var` for locals when the type is obvious.
- Default to `internal` for types and members unless wider API is required.
- On interfaces, always write explicit access modifiers on every member.
- On interfaces, always declare properties first, then methods.
- One type per file; file name = type name.
- No XML `/// summary` unless the folder already uses them.

## Conditions and loops

- Write `condition == false`, not `!condition`. Do not write `== true`.
- Use `!=` for inequality.
- Prefer `<` and `<=` over `>` and `>=` (invert when needed).
- Blank line before `if`, `for`, `foreach`, `while` when non-empty code precedes.
- Single-statement `if` / `for` / `foreach` body: no braces.
- Use `foreach` only when `for` is not practical.
- `for` index `i` is allowed; never shorten other names (`obj`, `ex`).

## Collections and exceptions

- Fields: `private readonly List<T> _items = new();`.
- Cache reused buffers in fields when used repeatedly.
- Catch: `Exception exception`, not `ex`.
- `Equals(object other)` — not `object obj`.

## Spacing and file layout

- `=` is ALWAYS surrounded by spaces (assignments, named arguments, logs, comparisons like `==` / `!=` already have spaces; never write `id={x}` or `a=b`).
- Blank line between consecutive members: fields group, constructor, properties, methods (never jam `}\n        public` / `}\n        internal`).
- File ALWAYS ends with a single trailing newline (last `}` then newline; editor shows an empty last line).

## Methods

- Methods use block body `{ }`; no expression-bodied methods (`=>`).
- Read-only properties may use `=>` when matching nearby mapper types.
- NEVER use optional parameters (`param = default`). ALL parameters are ALWAYS explicit at every call site.

## Enums

- First value is `None`, `Unknown`, or domain-neutral `= 0`.

## Config mappers

- Data-only: serialized/backing fields + read-only properties.
- No lookup methods on mappers; indexing in `*MapperManager`.
- Parsers: thin coordinator + dedicated parser per mechanic.

## DI constructor order

ASP.NET resolves by type; order is for readability.

**Layer order:** Infrastructure → Managers → Services → Factories.

- Within layer: alphabetical by type name.
- `private readonly` fields match ctor parameter order.
- Mutable runtime fields may precede readonly dependencies.

## Logging

- `ILogger<T>` via DI for errors and diagnostics.
- Tagged prefixes in messages when helpful (e.g. `[Story][Battle]`).
- Log calls are ALWAYS one line: `_logger.LogDebug($"...");` — never break the opening `(` onto the next line.

## Misc

- No emoji in comments, logs, or docs.
- No LINQ in runtime code.
- NEVER use abbreviations in code, logs, comments, or chat with the owner (write `damage over time`, not `DoT`; `data transfer object` only if forced by existing API names).
- NEVER use nullable reference types (`T?` for classes/interfaces, `out T?`, `null!`). Prefer index/`Try` patterns that do not need null.
- After generating code, re-read diff against these rules and neighboring files.
